{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03038",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.54,
      "end_seconds": 6.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Doctor? Hello, um, I hope this is the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.65,
      "end_seconds": 11.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.97,
      "end_seconds": 15.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.61,
      "end_seconds": 25.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "Mainly a severe headache for days. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.2,
      "end_seconds": 29.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.77,
      "end_seconds": 33.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Around two weeks, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 35.38,
      "end_seconds": 40.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Okay, so it was closer to three weeks, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.16,
      "end_seconds": 46.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.67,
      "end_seconds": 49.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.18,
      "end_seconds": 61.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.11,
      "end_seconds": 71.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "Lying down definitely sets it off. I'd give it a three, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.91,
      "end_seconds": 74.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.89,
      "end_seconds": 88.17,
      "duration_seconds": 11.28,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get double vision as well. I've also had drowsiness. As for drowsiness, it feels moderate to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.86,
      "end_seconds": 95.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Did you get weakness on one side, head injury or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.27,
      "end_seconds": 98.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.92,
      "end_seconds": 102.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.55,
      "end_seconds": 106.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.16,
      "end_seconds": 110.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.3,
      "end_seconds": 115.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.93,
      "end_seconds": 118.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.23,
      "end_seconds": 124.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.8,
      "end_seconds": 144.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 144.77,
      "end_seconds": 155.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.47,
      "text": "He takes escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day. He is on the contraceptive pill, daily, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.12,
      "end_seconds": 158.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "So, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.85,
      "end_seconds": 165.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.97,
      "end_seconds": 169.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Alright, any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.38,
      "end_seconds": 173.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Anxiety, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.88,
      "end_seconds": 179.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Okay, I can see anxiety in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.57,
      "end_seconds": 192.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.89,
      "end_seconds": 197.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "I'm allergic to grass pollen, I get sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.05,
      "end_seconds": 201.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Alright, I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.23,
      "end_seconds": 215.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.57,
      "end_seconds": 241.94,
      "duration_seconds": 9.37,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.8 degrees, height 176 centimetres, weight 93 kilos, pulse 88, blood pressure 146 over 100."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.46,
      "end_seconds": 244.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.37,
      "end_seconds": 249.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.72,
      "end_seconds": 277.23,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "From what you've told me, it fits best with possible cerebral venous thrombosis. Raised pressure in the head is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.84,
      "end_seconds": 280.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.19,
      "end_seconds": 316.22,
      "duration_seconds": 34.03,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with possible cerebral venous thrombosis do well once it's treated properly. I'll request an MRI of the head, it'll help with papilloedema. Let's get an urgent CT venogram, for possible venous thrombosis. Stop the pill, you need an urgent scan and admission. I'm going to send a referral to the neurology team. Let's plan a check straight away. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.97,
      "end_seconds": 320.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.68,
      "end_seconds": 324.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}